## 3. Internet — measure it, do not read it

**Measure the actual speeds. Do not record the advertised plan.** Upload is the binding constraint,
not download.

| | Advertised | **Measured** |
|---|---|---|
| Download | | ______ Mbps |
| Upload | | ______ Mbps |

| | |
|---|---|
| Provider | |
| Service type | ☐ Cable (asymmetric) ☐ Fibre (usually symmetric) ☐ Other |
| **Carrier-grade NAT?** | ☐ Yes ☐ No ☐ Not determined |
| Cellular signal at the property | ☐ Good ☐ Marginal ☐ Poor |

Carrier-grade address translation prevents direct tunnel establishment and forces a relayed
connection, which adds latency. Identify it now: at tier L and above it may require a static address
or a different service tier.

